   "he": "הָיָה בַּמִּזְרָח וְכָתַב בַּמַּעֲרָב: מַאן? אִילֵּימָא בַּעַל, הַיְינוּ ״שִׁינָּה שְׁמוֹ וּשְׁמָהּ, שֵׁם עִירוֹ וְשֵׁם עִירָהּ״!",
   "en": "§ It was stated in the mishna, that if «he was in the east and he wrote» the location in the bill of divorce as «in the west,» then the bill of divorce is invalid. The Gemara asks: «Who» is the mishna discussing? «If we say» that the place of the «husband» was changed, then «this is» the same as what is stated later on in the mishna: «He changed his name, or her name; the name of his city or the name of her city.»"
  }
